WEBVTT

00:00:00.711 --> 00:00:12.061
It's Tuesday morning at Wattlevale Logistics. One delivery on Sophie's run needs to go to Olivia Parker instead. From Oakfield Depot, dispatch can see which runs have left and which have returned.

00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:23.385
Here’s Olivia's morning run. Its colour connects her vehicle to her route, and her run sheet shows the last recorded position. Before moving the order, dispatch checks the area she covers.

00:00:25.014 --> 00:00:31.732
In Route Planning, Metro West is the delivery area. Open its postcode list to see which suburbs the fleet covers.

00:00:32.384 --> 00:00:39.412
The order cut-off for the morning shift is five thirty. That’s the deadline for orders to go on this shift. Let’s check who’s driving.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:49.677
The roster answers that for Tuesday, the tenth of November. Olivia is on duty. Opening her name shows her working week and the depot she starts from.

00:00:50.319 --> 00:00:57.504
Her run sheet is listed here too. That's the same run we saw on the map. Now the dispatcher can review the delivery that needs to move.

00:00:59.067 --> 00:01:08.252
Order Management opens on the fleet map. The warehouse anchors the routes. Let's open a delivery on Sophie Taylor's run and check its order before making a change.

00:01:08.903 --> 00:01:16.924
This is the order to move. Choose Reassign Order to see the eligible runs directly on the map. Olivia's name identifies the receiving route.

00:01:17.575 --> 00:01:26.460
Select Olivia. The plus signs mark the available places in her stop sequence. Choosing one tells the dispatcher exactly where the new delivery would fit.

00:01:27.112 --> 00:01:36.137
The dot marks the selected position. The review gives the stops on either side and the estimated change in kilometres and minutes. The order is still on Sophie's run.

00:01:36.788 --> 00:01:44.419
The dispatcher can compare an optimised sequence with the existing stop order. For this delivery, we'll keep Olivia's other stops in order.

00:01:45.071 --> 00:01:51.395
Apply the change. The confirmation is the point where the order moves. Let's follow that same order into tracking.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:02:00.646
In Order Status, search for the order we just moved. Opening the result brings up its delivery status and the run sheet that now owns it.

00:02:01.245 --> 00:02:08.436
Here it is on Olivia Parker's run. The stop number and route map give dispatch a way to check the change and answer a delivery enquiry.

00:02:10.105 --> 00:02:20.179
For a wider view, Insight reports on closed days. This is the previous reporting week. Open proof of delivery capture to see the fleet result and how it is calculated.

00:02:20.851 --> 00:02:31.180
Olivia’s Tuesday result opens the underlying stop records. Dispatch can see which deliveries have proof, just as it can trace today’s order from the warehouse to the driver responsible.

